    "result_text": "I agreed with and applied the finding.\n\n**Change** \u2014 `OwnerMapper.java`: added `import java.time.LocalDate;` and `import java.time.temporal.ChronoUnit;`, and rewrote the `membershipLevel` body to use the simple names:\n\n```java\nlong tenureDays = owner.getRegistrationDate() == null ? 0\n        : ChronoUnit.DAYS.between(owner.getRegistrationDate(), LocalDate.now());\n```\n\nThe finding was correct: the FQNs in the `@Mapping(expression = ...)` strings are required (MapStruct copies them verbatim into generated source, where imports don't apply), but this is an ordinary Java method body, so it should follow the file's convention of importing and using simple names \u2014 matching the existing `java.util.Collection`/`java.util.List` usage.\n\nTests pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`), so acceptance behaviour is intact.",
