    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: CHANGES REQUESTED\n\nThe core refactor is good and idiomatic: extracting the growing inline MapStruct expression into a named `default int membershipLevel(Owner)` sitting right next to the existing `hasEmail` default helper is exactly the right unit for this codebase, the expression now reads cleanly (`java(membershipLevel(owner))`), the javadoc mirrors the openapi description, and nothing is duplicated. One structural nit:\n\n- **Inline fully-qualified names break the file's own convention.** Inside `membershipLevel` the body uses `java.time.temporal.ChronoUnit.DAYS.between(...)` and `java.time.LocalDate.now()`. The FQNs in the `@Mapping(expression = ...)` strings are necessary \u2014 MapStruct emits those verbatim into generated code \u2014 but this is a normal Java method body, not an expression string. The file already imports `java.util.Collection`/`java.util.List` and refers to them by simple name, so a maintainer would expect `import java.time.LocalDate;` and `import java.time.temporal.ChronoUnit;` at the top and `ChronoUnit.DAYS.between(owner.getRegistrationDate(), LocalDate.now())` in the body. Add the imports and use the simple names to match surrounding code.",
